# Pin every text file to LF, so a Windows checkout is byte-identical to a
# Linux one. A CRLF shebang or a CRLF `set -euo pipefail` breaks shell
# scripts outright, and CRLF makes whole files show up as changed in diffs.
* text eol=lf

# Caveat for the one batch file: cmd.exe is only fully happy with CRLF once a
# .bat/.cmd starts using `goto :label`. agent/start-agent.bat has no labels,
# so LF is fine; should one ever need labels, give that single file an
# explicit `text eol=crlf` rule here (the last matching rule wins).

# Binary blobs are not text: never touch them.
*.bin  binary
*.png  binary
*.gz   binary
*.tgz  binary